6430.text:
The point 19.0°N, 81.0°E lies in central India — the Abujhmarh (Abujhmar Hills) region of Bastar, between Bijapur and Narayanpur districts in Chhattisgarh, roughly 8–10 km north of the Indravati River. This is unambiguously land (no ocean, lake, or ice shelf at these coordinates).

The surrounding terrain is the Bastar/Dandakaranya plateau: river valleys in the area sit near 300–350 m (the Indravati at Bhopalpatnam/Bijapur), while the dissected plateau and hill country just north of the valley rises to roughly 500–700 m (Narayanpur ~600 m, Jagdalpur ~555 m). Since the point is off the river valley floor and on the hilly plateau interior of the Abujhmarh, a bare-ground elevation around 550 m relative to EGM2008 is the best estimate.

