3657.text:
Based on the coordinates (49.0°N, 65.0°W), this point lies in the interior highlands of the Gaspé Peninsula (Gaspésie), Québec — in the eastern extension of the Chic‑Choc/Notre‑Dame (Appalachian) highlands, roughly between Murdochville and Gaspé, in the upland divide between the York/Dartmouth and Bonaventure river headwaters. This is land (no ocean or major lake at this exact point), so it is grounded terrain, not water.

The regional highland surface in this sector of the Gaspé interior sits on dissected Appalachian plateau/ridge terrain with ridge tops around 800–1000 m and intervening valleys around 400–550 m; a mid‑highland position near 49°N/65°W corresponds to roughly 700 m above sea level.

