3561.text:
Looking at coordinates **51.0°N, 103.0°E**: this falls in western Buryatia (Russia), in the mountainous intermontane region between the Dzhida river valley (Zakamensk, ~50.4°N/103.3°E, ~1000 m) to the south, the western spurs of the Khamar‑Daban and the Tunka depression (~51.6°N) to the north, and the Khövsgöl highlands (~1650 m) to the southwest. There are no major lakes or water bodies at this point — the area is a mountainous highland (Barguzin/Selenga middle‑mountain province) with ridges of ~1500–2000 m and valley floors of ~800–1000 m.

Therefore the surface is land (Solid), with a bare‑ground elevation in the order of ~1300 m above the EGM2008 geoid.

